{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1494313-shadowlands-and-the-loom","id":1494313,"title":"Shadowlands and the Loom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-04T08:08:21-07:00","id":1494313,"title":"Shadowlands and the Loom","content":"Sidereals use the Loom to track people in Creation, but what happens when a thaumaturge passes into a Shadowland at dawn or dusk? Would the Loom lose track completely, or would it pick them up again on returning to creation? Same for any companions. <br /> <br /> I am supposing that the Loom would track ghosts in Creation but not the Underworld, but I do not know that to be true. If a ghost passes into creation, would the thread for the person when they were alive restart, or would they get a new one?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T08:49:21-07:00","id":1494320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>L'het'esh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1494313-shadowlands-and-the-loom#post1494313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals use the Loom to track people in Creation, but what happens when a thaumaturge passes into a Shadowland at dawn or dusk? Would the Loom lose track completely, or would it pick them up again on returning to creation? Same for any companions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It picks them up again on return, if memory about the rules in the two past editions tricks me not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>L'het'esh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1494313-shadowlands-and-the-loom#post1494313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am supposing that the Loom would track ghosts in Creation but not the Underworld, but I do not know that to be true. If a ghost passes into creation, would the thread for the person when they were alive restart, or would they get a new one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically neither, since a ghost is dead, its fate already ran its course in life and now it's a being from outside (the Underworld), much like demons, fae and other such creatures of a nature connected to other realms of existence.<br /> <br /> <b>Unless</b> they have stayed in Creation for a continuous period between weeks and months, time in which the Loom might adjust to that being's &quot;waves&quot; upon the fates of creatures and things already in the Loom and weave it to some degree upon its purview and oversight. That in particular i remember from 2e, but could be based on 1e text that i now forget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T10:37:32-07:00","id":1494425,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}